{# NSSA with two ABRs (R2, R3): only one is elected translator (highest router-id - R3). Forcing
   `area 1 nssa translate type7 always` on R2, the non-elected ABR, makes R2 translate independently anyway -
   R1 then sees two separate type-5 LSAs for the same prefix, one from each ABR. A real production issue usually
   caused by copying the `always` keyword from a PE-CE MPLS/NSSA design onto a router that didn't need it.
   Self-contained: sets up NSSA on all three area-1 routers itself, independent of scenario 06. #}
{% if rollback %}
{% if target == "R4" %}
router ospf 1
 no redistribute connected
 no area 1 nssa
no route-map LO1-ONLY
{% elif target == "R2" %}
router ospf 1
 no area 1 nssa translate type7 always
 no area 1 nssa
{% else %}
router ospf 1
 no area 1 nssa
{% endif %}
{% else %}
{% if target == "R4" %}
route-map LO1-ONLY permit 10
 match interface Loopback1
router ospf 1
 area 1 nssa
 redistribute connected subnets route-map LO1-ONLY
{% elif target == "R2" %}
router ospf 1
 area 1 nssa
 area 1 nssa translate type7 always
{% else %}
router ospf 1
 area 1 nssa
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
